+# Summing cents
+
+`sum(values)` adds an array of nonnegative integer cents. For example,
+`sum([100, 200])` returns `300`. Zero entries are allowed, and an empty array
+returns `0`.
+
+A negative entry anywhere in the array throws `RangeError`, even when the
+overall total would be positive: `sum([100, -1, 200])` throws.
+
+Callers supply integer cents; this change does not add general input-type or
+integer validation.
